==In animation==
===''Pokémon the Series''===
===={{aniseries|DP}}====
Saturn first appeared in a brief cameo in ''[[DP036|A Secret Sphere of Influence!]]''. He later made full appearances in ''[[DP060|Journey to the Unown!]]'', where he obtained the [[Spear Key]] from the [[Solaceon Ruins]]; and ''[[DP096|Losing Its Lustrous!]]'', where he was able to steal the Adamant Orb.

Mars debuted in ''[[DP096|Losing Its Lustrous!]]'', while Jupiter debuted [[DP097|the next episode]]. Both of them, along with other members of Team Galactic, stole the Lustrous Orb from the [[Celestic Town Historical Research Center]], completing the pair they needed.

All three of them later appeared in ''[[DP110|Steeling Peace of Mind!]]'' and ''[[DP111|Saving the World From Ruins!]]'' where [[Mars]] was trying to help locate the [[Spear Pillar]] using the ruins on [[Iron Island]], however her mission brought {{Ash}} and {{ashfr}} onto the island. Eventually Mars was forced to abandon her original mission of scanning [[Mt. Coronet]] for the location of the [[Spear Pillar]], and switched her objective to destroying Iron Island. However, she failed to complete her mission due to [[Riley]] and [[Riley's Lucario|his Lucario]] using their [[aura]] to get rid of the explosion from the bombs that the Galactic Grunts had placed throughout Iron Island.

Charon made his debut as a cameo in ''[[DP111|Saving the World From Ruins!]]'', however he later appeared in ''[[DP136|Gateway to Ruin!]]'' where he, along with Saturn, were excavating Mt. Coronet to search for the entrance to the Spear Pillar. However, the ruins that they found were not what they were looking for and they proceeded to retreat.

In ''[[DP151|The Needs of the Three!]]'', with the help of [[J]], the three were able to obtain {{p|Mesprit}}, {{p|Azelf}} and {{p|Uxie}}, allowing the team to take control of them. This then allows them to summon {{p|Dialga}} and {{p|Palkia}}. However, they were later arrested after Cyrus disappeared, while Charon was nowhere to be seen.

===={{aniseries|JN}}====
Saturn, Jupiter, and Mars reappeared in [[Pokémon: The Arceus Chronicles]], having escaped from custody and planning to bring back [[Cyrus]], which resulted in a {{p|Heatran}} going on a rampage at [[Mount Coronet]] and threatening the [[Sinnoh]] region. They were later re-arrested.

==In the manga==
{{incomplete|section|The commanders in other manga, particularly Diamond and Pearl Adventure!}}
===Pokémon Adventures===
[[File:Galactic Commanders Adventures.png|thumb|240px|The commanders in Pokémon Adventures]]
===={{MangaArc|Diamond & Pearl}}====
Mars made her first appearance in ''[[PS344|Belligerent Bronzor]]'' where she attacked the [[Valley Windworks]] in an attempt to steal its energy. She battled {{adv|Diamond}}, {{adv|Pearl}}, and {{adv|Platinum}} and managed to escaped with the energy and a windmill that she later uses for transportation. Much later, she was assigned to capture {{p|Mesprit}} at [[Lake Verity]] and encountered Diamond there. She managed to capture Mesprit and assumed Diamond accidentally fell in the lake but he was later found to be hiding in the airship that had Mesprit captive.

Saturn makes his first appearance in ''[[PS349|Passing by Probopass and Maneuvering around Magnezone]]'' where he planned on capturing Platinum in order to get ransom money. He battle Platinum's bodyguards, [[Paka and Uji]], at the [[Lost Tower]] and is defeated, much to his anger and humiliation. Much later, at [[Lake Valor]], Saturn is assigned to capture {{p|Azelf}} and encounters Pearl there trying to protect it. Saturn defeats Pearl and successfully captures the Willpower Pokémon. 

Jupiter appears much later than the other two in ''[[PS395|Stopping Sableye]]'' where she is assigned to capture the Knowledge Pokémon, {{p|Uxie}}. At [[Lake Acuity]], she encounters Platinum, and the Gym Leaders of {{ci|Veilstone}} and {{ci|Snowpoint}}, [[Maylene]] and [[Candice]]. Jupiter easily defeats the three and manages to capture Uxie.

Charon is the last to appear, first appearing in ''[[PS401|Besting Buizel I]]''. He is responsible for the creation of the Red Chain. 

Sometime later, at the [[Spear Pillar]], the Commanders are seen waiting for their Boss, Cyrus so he can begin the ritual that will allow him to create a new world. While Cyrus goes to summon the legendary Pokémon, {{p|Dialga}} and {{p|Palkia}}, the Commanders are left behind to battle the intruders—the Gym Leaders of Sinnoh. Each of the Commanders fight two Gym Leaders each; Mars battles against [[Gardenia]] and [[Crasher Wake]], Saturn battles [[Roark]] and [[Fantina]], and Jupiter battles the revenge seekers, Candice and Maylene. Eventually, one by one the Commanders fall until none are left and the Gym Leaders go to battle Cyrus.

While Diamond, Pearl, Platinum, and [[Cynthia]] battle Cyrus on the top of the Spear Pillar, the Commanders are woken up by [[Sird]], who was previously shown to be a member of the [[Three Beasts]] of [[Team Rocket]]. Sird introduces herself to Mars and Saturn and reveals what she has been doing since her last appearance in the {{MangaArc|Emerald}}. Soon after, they are attacked by [[Riley]] who does battle with Sird, having tracked her with his aura sensing abilities. Sird and the Commanders eventually manage to escaped with plans of resurfacing sometime soon.

After the flight of other Commanders, Charon conspires the capture of Diamond's Regigigas but is captured. After {{p|Giratina}} takes the two Legendary Pokémon and Cyrus into the [[Distortion World]], Charon takes his leave.

===={{MangaArc|Platinum}}====
Charon is made the new leader of Team Galactic after Cyrus's disappearance. In ''[[PS432|The Final Dimensional Duel II]]'', the other Commanders are shown to be at [[Eterna City]], looking for their lost leader. They decide to enter the Distortion World through a hole that Giratina made. In ''[[PS436|The Final Dimensional Duel VI]]'', Charon has the Commanders battle [[Cheryl]], [[Mira]], and [[Marley]] while he makes his escape. They reunite with Cyrus in ''[[PS441|The Final Dimensional Duel XI]]'', where they resolve to follow him even when he disbands Team Galactic. 

===Pocket Monsters DP===
Only [[Mars]] and [[Charon]] appear in {{OBP|Pocket Monsters DP|Kosaku Anakubo}}, each making only one appearance.

